Z||000001||N_Man||10-13-2000||06:33 PM||||I cant tell buy looking (and im no familliar with the new mongoose) but is it a URT design. If it is Id stay away the benifits are few and it will ride like crap when compared to a new design.<P>If you didnt notice im a big fan of linkage suspension.  Specialized, Fisher, giant and trek(even though their warranty sucks).  These guys are my fav full suspentoins.<P>A note about mongoose (in canada, I dont know if the US company is the same)  Procycle makers of cheap bikes has bought out mongoose and turned them from a nice make into a wallmart bike.  Yes I can go to wallmart and buy a mongoose.  Just somthing to think about.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||10-16-2000||01:30 AM||||Linkage designs are great, but they also have alot more things to wear out, especially at the lower price points were they use bushings instead of bearings.  <P>If you're dead-set on getting a full suspension bike, I'd try to spend about $3-400 more than that.  That Mongoose doesn't have a lot going for it in terms of future upgradeability.  What you want most is a good frame, and that G3 only has straight-gauge 7005 aluminum frame.  It's alright if you're not doing any serious off-roading, but it'll be heavy and the component spec.. well.. pretty much sucks to tell ya the truth.  For $1200 you can get a sweet hardtail..  Or find out how much he can get the Mongoose Fairlane for, looks like a very sweet bike.. except for the hayes mechanical disc brakes..||||reg||1
